---
title: Smithy cipher
tags: tools
summary: >-
    A keyword cipher built on the Fibonacci sequence.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>It was made for private amusement, and was included in documents in The Da Vinci Code copyright case. <code class="tool-example">Hello</code> encrypted with the key <code class="tool-example">World</code> becomes <code class="tool-example">Rmxsp</code>.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithy_code" class="text-convrtr">Smithy code</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Smithy cipher", placeholder = "Example: Hello &srarr; World [key] &srarr; Rmxsp", actions = [{ id: filename + "Encrypt", label: "Encrypt" }, { id: filename + "Decrypt", label: "Decrypt" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Key"><span class="visually-hidden">Smithy </span>Key</label>
    <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Key" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
